ilya2@rcn.com wrote:

> When you read SoEA or cursed SoDA while confused, a randomly selected
> piece of armor gets fooproofed. Is it always selected from *among not
> yet fooproofed* pieces or not? 

No; from everything in the outer layer (so your armor can't be fooproofed
if you're wearing a cloak, or your shirt if you're wearing armor and/or a
cloak).

> IOW, is it possible to accidentally 
> "fireproof" something already fireproof?

Yes, eminently possible.

> At the moment, my wizard wears gauntlets of power and cursed fireproof
> +4 cloak of MR. I can not take off the cloak before rustproofing the
> gauntlets. Is there a chance a scroll will "fireproof" the cloak again
> instead?

Yes, a chance; it's 1 in [number of pieces or armor in outer layer]. That
is, 1/2 if this is all you're wearing; if you're also wearing a helmet
and boots it's 1/4.

> As an aside, does fireproofing protect cloth/leather items from brown
> pudding attacks?

Yes, it does.

